1ehl|v|of Obligate	d:1bxn,116,4;16kt,91,3~1bxn,116,4;16kt,91,3
1ehn|n|The act of obligating. ; That which obligates or constrains; the binding power of a promise, contract, oath, or vow, or of law; that which constitutes legal or moral duty. ; Any act by which a person becomes bound to do something to or for anouther, or to forbear something; external duties imposed by law, promise, or contract, by the relations of society, or by courtesy, kindness, etc. ; The state of being obligated or bound; the state of being indebted for an act of favor or kindness; as, to place others under obligations to one. ; A bond with a condition annexed, and a penalty for nonfulfillment. In a larger sense, it is an acknowledgment of a duty to pay a certain sum or do a certain things.	a:1bxb,92,7;q4m,79,8;16kl,70,9~16kl,70,9;q4m,79,8;1bxb,92,7
